Given-When-Then Acceptance Criteria
These should test the actual behavior of the system.

- Acceptance Criterion 1 — Matching Clubs
Given the system contains verified clubs matching the user's search criteria, 
When the user searches using those criteria, 
Then the system shall display the matching clubs.

- Acceptance Criterion 2 — No Results
Given there are no verified clubs matching the user's search criteria, 
When the user performs the search, 
Then the system shall display a message indicating that no matching clubs were found.

- Acceptance Criterion 3 — View Club Information
Given a search returns one or more clubs,
When the user selects a club from the search results,
Then the system shall display the club's available information, including its description and designated contact information.

- Acceptance Criterion 4 — Broadening Search
Given a user's search returns no results, 
When the user changes or removes one or more search criteria and searches again, 
Then the system shall perform the revised search and display any matching clubs.

- Acceptance Criterion 5 — Only Verified Clubs
Given both verified and unverified clubs exist in the system, 
When a user searches for clubs, 
Then the search results shall contain only verified clubs.
